            <ArticleTitle>Spontaneous coronary artery spasm during coronary angiography in a patient with exercise-induced ST segment elevation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>720-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a patient with a history of early morning chest pain who developed ST segment elevation during a treadmill exercise test. Severe coronary artery stenosis was identified initially and was relieved after intracoronary administration of nitroglycerin. A history of vasospastic angina in this patient facilitated prompt diagnosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
